+# Performance history
+
+## UserPromptSubmit read path
+
+The repository does not record a measured full-recall p95 for the
+`UserPromptSubmit` hook on the adversarial synthetic 30-word vocabulary before
+the term-selection fix. It therefore cannot be reported here without inventing
+a number.
+
+The fix was to select at most eight prompt terms by inverse document frequency
+(IDF), dropping terms absent from the store and, for stores with at least 50
+records, terms present in more than one third of records. This keeps ubiquitous
+terms and their long posting lists out of the FTS5 query.
+
+The repository also does not record a measured full-recall p95 for that same
+adversarial 30-word-vocabulary workload after the fix, so no post-fix number is
+claimed here. The nearby measurements are not substitutes: the evidence log's
+35.53 ms and 8.75 ms p95 values measure the BM25 stage for 24-first-term and
+top-eight-IDF queries, respectively, while the documented 4.31 ms p95 measures
+the complete hook on a different ordinary full-recall prompt.
